# Working on [[.Name]]

Read README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md and native CI before editing. Use Go 1.27.3,
GOWORK=off and published dependencies without sibling replacements.

- This is an application-owned single-module [[.Layout]] skeleton using [[.Transport]].
- Keep dependency assembly explicit in app.go; do not introduce a DI container
  without an application decision. Commands parse configuration; service Run owns
  assembly and lifecycle. infrastructure/server only constructs transports.
- Add contexts and services on demand. Services inherit transport configuration
  from the server constructors; no duplicate project metadata is stored.
- Native HTTP add api creates one private adapter, without Proto or generation.
  Implement authorization and application calls, then mount the route explicitly.
[[if .GRPC]]- Use add api --transport grpc or gateway for Proto contracts. Gateway requires
  HTTP and gRPC. Run task api ACTION=generate and go mod tidy after contract changes.
- api scaffold fills missing unary methods offline, preserving existing implementations.
  It does not scaffold streams, HTTP bindings, use cases or placeholder tests.
- Proto and HTTP options are authoritative; never edit api/gen/go or generated OpenAPI.
  Run task api for contract drift and task api ACTION=breaking with an explicit Git baseline.
- Preserve authenticated gRPC, request limits, safe errors and cancellation.
[[end]]- Keep domain/application transport-free. Convert requests/responses in private adapters.
- Use narrow consumer-owned ports and actual CQRS use cases. Choose middleware at assembly.
- Maintain literal loopback listener defaults. New HTTP routes need explicit identity,
  authorization, input limits and safe errors. Test real behavior rather than placeholders.
- Agent tools and authorization are application-owned. Model endpoints come only from
  trusted startup configuration. Preserve runner capacity, deadline and token limits.
- doctor reads project/tool state; it never installs tools, fetches modules or writes files.
- New/add operations are offline, root-confined and refuse overwrites. Honor .nostosx.lock;
  never remove another active writer's lock. Preserve rollback of owned additions.
- Run task check INTEGRATION=true, lint and vulncheck[[if .GRPC]], plus task api[[end]].
- Never commit, push, tag or deploy without explicit user authorization.
